title: Suspicious Microsoft 365 Session Cookie Replay via AiTM Proxy
id: 8a3c1f72-4b9e-4d6a-a8c3-7e2f5d9b1c4a
status: experimental
description: Detects patterns consistent with adversary-in-the-middle proxy phishing (e.g. Evilginx2/BigBear 2.0) where stolen session cookies are replayed from anomalous IP addresses or geographic locations to access Microsoft 365 services without completing MFA.
references:
  - https://databreaches.net/2026/09/07/bigbear-microsoft-365-phishing-service-bypassed-mfa-at-258-organizations/
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026-09-08
tags:
  - attack.t1557
  - attack.t1539
logsource:
  product: cloud
  service: office365
detection:
  selection_auth:
    EventSource: AzureActiveDirectory
    EventOperation: Sign-in
    ResultType: 0
  selection_anomaly:
    ResultStatus: Success
    MfaDetail: null
    DeviceDetail: contains 'Browser'
  selection_vpn_or_proxy:
    IPAddress: contains 'Vultr'
    OR IPAddress: contains 'The Constant Company'
    OR LocationInfo: contains 'VPN'
  condition: selection_auth and selection_anomaly and selection_vpn_or_proxy
falsepositives:
  - Legitimate VPN or proxy usage by remote workers
  - Corporate network egress through shared IP ranges
level: medium
